[SOURCE BINDING AND SELECTION LAW]
source_binding_status: PASS
selection_law_status: PASS

The structural SourceContext validator validates concrete BSEP, Replay, G2-A,
and G2-B source-family object geometry. The contextual Router validator then
rebuilds each committed binding from the actual source objects and compares
the complete binding and snapshot geometry. A copied PASS label, copied
digest, ID-only match, absent source, or caller-selected binding state is not
accepted.

BSEP inspection uses the current business-request, route-packet, semantic
proposal, structured-rationale, and bounded evidence validators. Replay uses
the current evidence profile, sealed package, external anchor, and sealed
Replay validators. G2-A uses the current present-eligibility inspection and
requires the complete positive predicate, including retry_eligible=false.
G2-B validates the address, temporal query, records, evaluations, candidates,
resolution plan/descent, Root shortcut, certificate, report, and compatibility
family applicable to the binding state.

Request identity and transaction identity remain independent. For applicable
G2-B cases, the Router transaction is required to equal the actual
builder-derived TemporalQuery query_id. No literal replacement transaction is
accepted.

Feasibility is established before cost. Executable selection uses the exact
ordered key (safe_depth_rank, expected_cost_units, canonical_mode_index).
Hard block and missing required user input are applied before executable
feasibility; blocked has global precedence, needs_user owns the missing-input
terminal, and no-safe-mode selects blocked. request_class, scope_class, and
risk_class are absent from feasibility and selection authority. No public
transition evaluator accepts caller guard tuples, rule IDs, reasons, or commit
booleans.

